WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:33.910
You may ask yourself: What does Dwayne ‘The
Rock’ Johnson and his charismatic personality

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:40.620
have to do with a video about One Piece? After
all you can´t really say that these two topics

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:46.160
are too closely related, right?
But what if I told you that the Rock and One

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:51.070
Piece DO have something in common. Or rather
that there is a character in the story of

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:57.820
One Piece that closely resembles Johnson in
more than just one way.

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:03.860
Franky is without a doubt one of the more
flashy characters in the story. At first glance,

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:08.810
comparing him to the Rock may seem a little
superficial, but I promise you that it will

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:14.369
all make sense, once we make it to the end
of this video. So, bear with me here.

00:01:14.369 --> 00:01:19.770
To be completely honest with you, I personally
didn't really like Franky as a character too

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:26.280
much for quite some time. And I can’t really
tell you why. Maybe it was his unusual character

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:32.240
design or his rowdy-like language that didn´t
speak to me, but I simply couldn’t enjoy

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:37.750
him as a character as much as I did the other
straw hats at that time. And then, as a grew

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:43.009
older and got more and more involved with
One Piece, I noticed something weird. I caught

00:01:43.009 --> 00:01:48.259
myself liking the chapters and scenes with
Franky more and more and before I knew it,

00:01:48.259 --> 00:01:53.821
I thought that he was actually an amazing
character. How the hell did that happen? As

00:01:53.821 --> 00:01:58.630
I came to realize, my mistake was, that I
thought that Franky was designed to appeal

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:04.780
to younger readers. And in a certain way that
is probably true. But the way his character

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:11.070
is designed actually resonates a lot more
with my older self. So, let´s find out who

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:20.910
Franky the Cyborg truly is and why Oda might
have written the Rock into One Piece by accident.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:26.629
Franky is a powerfully built, tall man with
a height of at least seven feet…or a little

00:02:26.629 --> 00:02:31.700
over 2 meters in case you´re like me and
don´t know how much that is. An immediate

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:37.790
eyecatcher are Franky´s forearms, which are
enormously big while his biceps are comparatively

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:44.150
small. The same goes for his muscular upper
body, with unproportionally thin legs. He

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:50.019
has brightly-colored blue hair and blue star
tattoos on his forearms. Going with his existence

00:02:50.019 --> 00:02:55.439
as a cyborg, he has a very geometric looking
face with a metallic nose and a triangular

00:02:55.439 --> 00:03:01.879
chin. His choice of clothing usually comprises
of speedos and an open Hawaiian "Aloha" shirt

00:03:01.879 --> 00:03:07.370
with a large golden chain necklace around
his neck. Before becoming a cyborg, Franky

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:13.620
went half-naked simply because he felt like
it. Now however, his cyborg body is built

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:19.249
in a way that covering himself up would actually
limit him in using his technical features,

00:03:19.249 --> 00:03:25.469
that include a variety of weapons and other,
let´s say interesting features? Also, he

00:03:25.469 --> 00:03:30.569
only wears a shirt to cover his back, the
only part of his body he cannot reach and

00:03:30.569 --> 00:03:36.329
modify and as a result is most vulnerable
to damage. To make his character even more

00:03:36.329 --> 00:03:40.330
quirky and round things up, his body runs
entirely on cola.

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:43.989
Next to Robin, Franky is the only other Straw
Hat that initially started out as an antagonist

00:03:43.989 --> 00:03:49.020
for the crew. Franky grew up on Water 7 as
an orphaned boy from the south blue, where

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:54.779
he was thrown overboard by his parents, who
also were pirates, when he was barely 4 years

00:03:54.779 --> 00:04:00.769
old. He was found by the legendary shipwright
Tom, who took him in and made him his apprentice.

00:04:00.769 --> 00:04:06.829
Franky´s REAL name is Cutty Flam, but his
fellow apprentice Iceburg decided to nickname

00:04:06.829 --> 00:04:12.450
him Franky and the name stuck ever since.
When Tom was arrested for building the Oro

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:17.200
Jackson for the pirate king Gol D. Roger,
he managed to evade his sentence by offering

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:21.820
to build a Sea Train in order to help the
struggling city. Together with Iceburg and

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:28.191
Franky he managed to finish the train in time.
However, Spandam, an official of the World

00:04:28.191 --> 00:04:33.770
Government, framed Tom for attacking Water
7 using Franky´s own personal fleet of mini

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:39.010
battle ships, that he had built to fight off
the sea kings. His goal was to get his hands

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:44.100
on the blueprints of the ancient weapon Pluton,
that was in Tom´s possession.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:49.610
When Tom was taken to Enies Lobby on the Sea
Train, Franky tried to stand in its path and

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:56.290
was run over. Heavily injured, he drifted
to a ship where he modified his own body into

00:04:56.290 --> 00:05:02.410
a cyborg and returned to Water Seven several
years later. He revealed himself to Iceburg,

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:07.420
who was now the mayor of the prospering Water
Seven. From him Franky received the plans

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:13.190
for the Pluton, and he decided to protect
Iceburg and Water 7 from the shadows. To do

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:19.690
so, he became a ship dismantler, bounty hunter
and thug and form the Franky Family, taking

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:26.850
in cast outs from the city. So now that we
know Franky´s crazy and tragic story, let´s

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:32.880
look at his character.
Franky has been filled with positive characteristics

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:39.340
by Oda, that maybe aren´t apparent at first
glance. But let´s start with a more obvious

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:45.440
one: Franky has shown us over and over again
how strong-willed he is. And he takes it to

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:51.350
the utmost extreme, by performing self-surgery
and modification on himself while he was at

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:57.280
the verge of death, after being run over by
the sea train. This is a feat that maybe even

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:04.110
a Luffy or Zoro would have difficulties with,
regardless of the technical knowledge involved.

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:09.170
Hand in hand with this go his craftiness,
his sharp wit and his creativity that make

00:06:09.170 --> 00:06:15.930
him such a unique shipwright. Franky is one
of the very few people that are able to create

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:21.890
and handle technology on an advanced level.
Not only is his cyborg technology incredibly

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:27.900
advanced, but he also had no problem understanding
and integrating Dr. Vegapunk inventions during

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:33.410
the time skip.
Franky also has a very free-spirited and eccentric

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:38.900
personality. He is proud to be who he is,
with all his quirks and unique features and

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:44.270
doesn´t like to follow social norms let alone
the law of the world government. This also

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:49.170
reflects really well in his language that
is kind of punky and includes him rolling

00:06:49.170 --> 00:07:00.130
his R.
Another side of Franky that often gets overlooked

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:05.700
is his altruism and kindness towards others.
Whether it is with the children on Punk Hazard

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:11.560
or the Tontatta on Dressrosa, our Cyborg clearly
cares, not only for his crew and family but

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:17.350
also those around him in general. This is
closely related to his emotional side, that

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:21.310
makes him tear up very quickly when hearing
a tragic story.

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:25.790
Most importantly though, and I think this
is one of the core messages of this video,

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:32.230
Franky is actually incredibly mature, despite
all his goofiness. When stopping the sea train,

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:37.560
he shouts that he wants to be like his father
figure Tom. Someone who took him in, even

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:42.370
after his parents abandoned him. So that´s
what he did. He went through the streets of

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:47.950
Water 7 and took in those people who had been
forgotten by everyone else. He gave them a

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:53.670
family and a place to belong. We can also
see this in Franky´s relationship with everyone

00:07:53.670 --> 00:07:59.490
in the crew. He takes on the role of a kind
of father or big brother for especially the

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:04.730
younger ones, teaching Usopp about engineering,
taking care of Chopper and supporting those

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:09.940
who need him, like Luffy in Dressrosa and
Robin in Enies Lobby. While we often see him

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:14.590
goofing around and entertaining the crew,
he always seems to keep serious matters in

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:19.160
mind. And his world view in general is one
of the most mature in the crew as well. I

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:24.990
think this maturity was something that I didn´t
manage to see when I was younger, and it explains

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:29.251
why I came to love Franky as a character a
little later than some of the other Straw

00:08:29.251 --> 00:08:35.310
Hats. It seems to go against his character
and yet, when you look at the big picture

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:40.169
fits perfectly.
Interestingly enough, this maturity also reflects

00:08:40.169 --> 00:08:47.079
in Franky´s drivers for character development.
Because in a way, he truly is already matured.

00:08:47.079 --> 00:08:52.340
His only real inner need is his inability
to forgive himself for the death of his master

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:57.850
Tom. Otherwise Franky doesn´t really have
anything he has to change I order to become

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:03.579
a better person. Yes, he indeed did do some
immoral things, like beating Usopp or stealing

00:09:03.579 --> 00:09:09.149
from pirates like the straw hats. But he mostly
did all of those out of a sense of atonement

00:09:09.149 --> 00:09:14.949
and love. In memory of Tom, he decided to
spend the rest of his days on Water 7, attacking

00:09:14.949 --> 00:09:19.769
incoming thieves and looters, organizing all
the thugs so that he could keep the city´s

00:09:19.769 --> 00:09:24.079
crime in check and overall protecting the
city that Tom loved so much.

00:09:24.079 --> 00:09:30.269
Franky´s dream on the other hand is really
hands on: He wanted to create a dream ship

00:09:30.269 --> 00:09:35.800
out of Adam Wood and see it sail around the
world. In other words, Franky is literally

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:41.089
living his dream with the straw hats at the
moment. At the same time, he strives to become

00:09:41.089 --> 00:09:46.209
stronger to be able to protect his friends
on their dangerous journey. No wonder then

00:09:46.209 --> 00:09:54.060
that Franky values family and kindness as
much as he values freedom and of course craftsmanship.

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:58.290
How then does this impressive cyborg of a
man influence the story?

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:03.879
Being the shipwright of the straw hats, Franky
is the one enabling the crew to sail on the

00:10:03.879 --> 00:10:08.249
dangerous waters of the grand line in the
first place. He was the one who built the

00:10:08.249 --> 00:10:12.889
Sunny and also is the one to repair her and
keep her in good shape over the course of

00:10:12.889 --> 00:10:18.550
their journey. In other words: Franky quite
literally is responsible for moving the plot

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:25.160
along. Apart from his duties as a craftsman
though, he also is an important fighting asset,

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:29.959
when things get a little heated. And more
often than not, he actually plays a major

00:10:29.959 --> 00:10:35.589
role in events taking place. On Enies Lobby,
he helped the Straw Hats save Robin. As a

00:10:35.589 --> 00:10:39.930
matter of fact, he was the one to unchain
and protect her until the rest of the crew

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:45.420
arrived. And later he helped everyone escape
by using a Coup de Vent, blowing the blockade

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:49.540
of buster call ships apart and sending the
Going Merry flying through the air. But he

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:50.540
also knows how to support his fighting friends,
as we could see on Dressrosa, where he took

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:53.110
care of Luffy during his fight with Doflamingo.
Another detail, that is often forgotten, is

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:58.300
that Franky most likely still holds the knowledge
of how to rebuild the ancient weapon Pluton.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:03.990
A plot point that might well become relevant
again down the line. And finally, in terms

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:09.129
of character development, he also provides
guidance for the younger crew members, helping

00:11:09.129 --> 00:11:13.870
them feeling safe and comfortable on this
dangerous journey. In that context, it is

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:18.809
of course also worth looking at Franky´s
own character arc.

00:11:18.809 --> 00:11:24.540
Since Franky has a very mature and as a result
nearly complete character, his development

00:11:24.540 --> 00:11:30.189
over the course of the story is rather minor
and altruistic. Franky definitely still is

00:11:30.189 --> 00:11:35.149
working on overcoming his guilt regarding
Tom´s death, but it is nothing that Oda puts

00:11:35.149 --> 00:11:41.079
too much into focus for us. Still, we can
see Franky making progress in this regard,

00:11:41.079 --> 00:11:46.689
be it defeating Spandam, who was responsible
for his pain, joining the straw hats, meeting

00:11:46.689 --> 00:11:51.910
Tom´s brother Dan on Fishman Island or simply
fulfilling his dream, sailing with his friends.

00:11:51.910 --> 00:11:58.009
It is a very low-key, but nonetheless fulfilling
change of character, that I hope will be brought

00:11:58.009 --> 00:12:02.550
up again at one point in the story.
For his character as a whole, I feel like

00:12:02.550 --> 00:12:07.589
there are three arcs in particular where Franky
was at the center of events. The first one

00:12:07.589 --> 00:12:14.080
is obviously the Water 7 and Enies Lobby arc.
And yes, that is also Robin´s big arc, no

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:19.269
doubt about it. But that Oda managed to make
it the major point of events for not just

00:12:19.269 --> 00:12:25.350
one but TWO straw hats, just confirms for
me how great this arc truly was. Starting

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:31.199
out as antagonists, Luffy and Franky came
to forgive and trust each other over the course

00:12:31.199 --> 00:12:36.680
of events. And after all they went through
together, in the end there really was no other

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:41.259
option for either of them to not journey together
from then on out.

00:12:41.259 --> 00:12:46.949
The time skip was another confirmation about
how important Franky would be for the crew.

00:12:46.949 --> 00:12:52.350
Stranded on the island of Karakuri, the hometown
of the infamous Dr. Vegapunk, he was able

00:12:52.350 --> 00:12:57.329
to further improve himself as well as the
sunny. All that for the sake of protecting

00:12:57.329 --> 00:13:01.879
his friends and making the Sunny into a ship
of dreams for the crew.

00:13:01.879 --> 00:13:07.749
Finally, Franky got to play a major role in
the events unfolding on Dressrosa, where not

00:13:07.749 --> 00:13:12.889
only he showed true bravery and kindness in
protecting the Tontatta and Luffy, but also

00:13:12.889 --> 00:13:18.680
had an ideologically amazing fight against
Senor Pink of the Donquixote family. Franky

00:13:18.680 --> 00:13:24.029
may not seem like it at first glance, but
he truly is a fantastic character, that is

00:13:24.029 --> 00:13:29.839
much more complex and contributes much more
to the plot than one would think.

00:13:29.839 --> 00:13:36.129
So why the Rock? I hope by now you already
have a feeling what I´m talking about here.

00:13:36.129 --> 00:13:41.529
Because Franky and Dwayne Johnson actually
share a lot of similarities, and in more than

00:13:41.529 --> 00:13:47.459
one way. Let´s start with some of the more
obvious ones. I personally think that both

00:13:47.459 --> 00:13:53.269
Franky AND the Rock are extremely likable
characters. They both have a very positive

00:13:53.269 --> 00:13:59.190
aura around them and basically ooze energy
and motivation. Then of course there is the

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:02.940
look. [Franky next to the Rock] I mean c´mon.
If these guys don´t look similar I don´t

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:08.250
know. Beside the thing with the glasses, which
I found super hilarious once I realized it

00:14:08.250 --> 00:14:14.350
by the way, thy both have the bulky, muscular
‘Strong Man’ look. They also both have

00:14:14.350 --> 00:14:19.629
a connection to Hawaii and Oda actually stated
that Franky would be American, if One Piece

00:14:19.629 --> 00:14:24.869
took place in the real world. I mean these
are minor things, but I just feel like they

00:14:24.869 --> 00:14:30.490
round off the analogy quite well.
Then of course we have their upbringing. Both

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:35.389
had a difficult childhood. But they also managed
to work their way out of there through their

00:14:35.389 --> 00:14:40.249
enthusiasm and positivity and finally managed
to lead a life that brings them happiness

00:14:40.249 --> 00:14:44.379
every day.
Finally, I feel like they also resemble each

00:14:44.379 --> 00:14:50.459
other immensely in their personality. Both
strongly value kindness and humor and both

00:14:50.459 --> 00:14:56.279
are extremely eccentric and free-spirited.
Now that I think about it, in a way they even

00:14:56.279 --> 00:15:01.551
resemble each other in the way they changed
over the years. Pre-time skip Franky, with

00:15:01.551 --> 00:15:07.309
his rowdy-like appearance really reminds me
of a younger wrestling-Rock, while post-time

00:15:07.309 --> 00:15:13.240
skip Franky is closer to the Dwayne Johnson
today. Mature, altruistic and somehow looking

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:19.980
more like a tank than before. So, there you
have it. With Franky, Oda has created a truly

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:27.100
amazing character and by accident he might
have made the Rock join the straw hats.

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:41.529
Hey everybody. Thank you so much for watching.
Making this video turned out to be a lot more

00:15:41.529 --> 00:15:47.059
fun than I expected. I really enjoy making
all of these videos, but for Franky I just

00:15:47.059 --> 00:15:51.040
kept coming across these small details that
I just found so fascinating.

